{
 "format": 1,
 "comment": "The random boxes. A box type has an id, a title, a colour, how likely each kind of zombie is to drop it ('drop': common, special, brute, and 'map' for one a map leaves lying about), and its outcomes. An outcome has a weight, a title shown to everybody, a message ({name} is whoever opened it), and a list of actions. Every action's 'do' and its parameters are documented in game/zz_boxes.gd (the _do_ methods); an action this game does not know refuses the whole file at load, naming it. 'who' picks whom a survivor action touches: opener (default), team, others, near (radius), random, nearest (count), downed, dead. Effects from 'pace', 'damage_boost' and the like stack: two that each double something make it four times. SCHEMA (all optional, read by ZzBoxes._read_schema): 'polarity' positive|negative|mixed; 'impact' self|radius|everyone|game (who an 'effect' action lands on); 'radius' metres for impact radius; 'stacks' true|false and 'max_stacks' (a repeat of a non-stacking effect only lengthens it; a stacking one counts up to the cap, then lengthens); 'duration' {mode: instant|seconds|round, min, max} drawn uniformly each time the box is opened (seconds), or until the round ends (round); 'survives_round' true lets a game-impacting effect outlast the round's end; 'params' is the handler's own. A named box is one outcome {\"do\": \"effect\", \"name\": <handler in ZzBoxes.HANDLERS>}. The eight random boxes keep their own per-action 'seconds'; their schema is descriptive.",
